# Ibiza Villas 2000 — agent conventions

This build follows a strict mu-plugin + thin theme architecture. These
rules apply to every change unless a brief explicitly overrides them.

## Architecture

- All custom logic lives in `wp-content/mu-plugins/ibv-core/`.
- The theme `wp-content/themes/ibv/` is presentation only — no business
  logic, no ACF registration, no post type registration.
- Each new feature is a folder under `mu-plugins/ibv-core/includes/`,
  required from `bootstrap.php` in load order.
- ACF groups are registered in PHP, hooked to `acf/init`. Never use
  `acf-json/` sync. One file per group under `includes/acf/`.
- ACF field placement follows ownership: content consumed by a **single
  page** lives on that page's template field group (`get_field('x')`);
  content consumed by **two or more pages/surfaces** lives on Site Options
  (`get_field('x', 'option')`). A page may still override a global default
  by passing a page-level value into a shared section (e.g. Booking
  Confirmation's own 3-step cards). Don't put single-page content in Site
  Options.

## Naming

- PHP functions / classes prefixed `ibv_` (or `ibv_core_` for helpers
  callable from templates).
- CSS uses BEM with `ibv-` prefix; utilities `ibv-u-*`.
- Text domain `'ibv'`.
- File names kebab-case.
- ACF: group keys `group_ibv_{scope}`; field keys `field_ibv_{scope}_{name}`.

## CSS

- Plain CSS, no build step.
- All values reference custom-property tokens defined in
  `mu-plugins/ibv-core/assets/css/tokens.css`. No hardcoded colours, font
  sizes, spacing, radius, motion.
- Component CSS is co-located with the component PHP. Each component
  registers its own handle in `shared-assets.php` and enqueues itself
  conditionally inside its helper function.

## Output

- Escape every output: `esc_html()`, `esc_url()`, `esc_attr()`,
  `wp_kses_post()`.
- Translate user-facing strings: `__( 'text', 'ibv' )`.
- Images: always `ibv_core_image()` or `wp_get_attachment_image()`.
  Never raw `<img>`.
- Buttons: always `ibv_core_button()`. Never raw `<a class="button">`.
- Section headings: `ibv_core_section_heading()` for eyebrow + title combos.

## Editor

- Classic editor only. Block editor is disabled site-wide via
  `includes/editor.php`. CPTs registered by this mu-plugin opt out via
  `show_in_rest => false`.
- If a future brief needs the block editor for a specific post type,
  narrow the filter in `editor.php` rather than dropping it altogether.

## Dependencies

- ACF Pro is the only required plugin.
- No new npm or composer dependencies without explicit approval in the
  brief. No build step.
